1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:08,084
Main frame P1–P3: complete outer edges, ending 1600, 1601 and 1601.

2
00:00:08,539 --> 00:00:13,454
Roof R1–R2: complete outer edges, ending 1640.

3
00:00:13,908 --> 00:00:18,263
Beam X: heartwood ending 1530 and a redundant joint.

4
00:00:18,724 --> 00:00:23,789
Pause to compare date groups with member positions and identify evidence that could support

5
00:00:23,803 --> 00:00:26,136
repair or reuse.

6
00:00:26,939 --> 00:00:31,828
The sampled main-frame arrangement cannot be completed before 1601.

7
00:00:32,283 --> 00:00:37,310
The 1640 roof timbers suggest a later intervention to investigate.

8
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:43,106
X is a reuse candidate; missing outer wood and other explanations remain.

9
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:48,849
Use the exercise to compare supported explanations and unresolved points rather than to

10
00:00:48,862 --> 00:00:52,036
declare a complete historical narrative.

11
00:00:52,839 --> 00:00:56,511
Dendroprovenancing compares candidate source regions.

12
00:00:56,973 --> 00:01:00,611
The best match need not identify a unique origin.

13
00:01:01,065 --> 00:01:05,861
Consider reference coverage, timber trade, species and anatomy.

14
00:01:06,315 --> 00:01:11,137
A regional chronology match does not by itself establish timber origin.

15
00:01:11,591 --> 00:01:16,520
Consider broad climate coherence and the available reference coverage.

16
00:01:17,323 --> 00:01:23,831
Mitsutani (2001) reports a 594 CE date for the central pillar.

17
00:01:24,286 --> 00:01:29,424
Three further outer rings extend the measured sequence ending in 591.

18
00:01:29,878 --> 00:01:33,602
What evidence connects a member date to the date of the building?.

19
00:01:33,904 --> 00:01:38,983
Consult the primary report for material condition, the event constrained and the wording of

20
00:01:38,996 --> 00:01:43,284
its conclusion, rather than filling gaps from a summary.

21
00:01:44,087 --> 00:01:49,996
Complete sapwood in one sample supports winter 1522/23 felling.

22
00:01:50,458 --> 00:01:55,563
The report suggests construction in 1523 or within a year or two.

23
00:01:56,023 --> 00:01:59,991
Separate the felling result from the construction interpretation.

24
00:02:00,445 --> 00:02:06,142
Reports in another language can be read using the same checks: material, measurement, dating

25
00:02:06,155 --> 00:02:09,136
evidence and structural context.
